    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22851" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-dĭsertus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not eloquent</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Academicus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 2, 1, 1</span></i>
			.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Of inanim. and abstr. things: prudentia,</span>”
				<i>at a loss for words</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 35, 142</span></i>
			.— <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indĭsertē</span></b> , <i>not eloquently</i> (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orationem non indiserte collaudavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Q. Fr. 2, 1, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
